<sn><md>### Human Health Consequences of Mutagenic Pollutants

- Cancer Risk: Long-term exposure to airborne or waterborne mutagens directly contributes to lung, skin, liver, and bladder cancers.

- Heritable Genetic Defects: Germ-cell mutations can be passed down to future generations, increasing the prevalence of inherited metabolic or developmental disorders.

- Neurological and Hormonal Disruption: Heavy metals and organic pollutants damage central nervous system pathways and interfere with
the endocrine system.</md></sn>